                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">07/Jul/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-10002"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Incident report:(192.168.189.128) local system execution at <span class="error">&#91;Time&#93;</span>. Administrative backup mechanism destruction routine detected. Detected by Splunk (EventCode 1), Wazuh (Rule 92651), and local process auditing. Deletion of Volume Shadow Copies initiated.<br/>
Active Response: Host Lockdown Triggered. Severity: CRITICAL.</p>

<p>Time of Activity: <tt>2026-07-06</tt> at 11:45</p>

<p>Reason for classifying as true positive: Verified the active process creation event logs inside the Splunk SIEM workspace. Telemetry records show the administrative binary 'vssadmin.exe' running with argument variables specifically set to 'delete shadows /all /quiet'. This exact execution layout is signature behavior used exclusively by modern ransomware strains to inhibit operating system recovery.</p>

<p>Reason for escalating the alert: Found critical post-exploitation modifications designed to compromise host integrity and prevent system rollbacks. The malicious logic maps directly to the MITRE ATT&amp;CK framework technique T1490 (Inhibit System Recovery) verified cleanly using Sysmon Event Code 1.</p>

<p>Recommended Remediation Actions: Trigger an emergency host containment response via Wazuh/Jira orchestration, terminate the active parent process ID, run a file integrity baseline scan on the 'C:\SOC_Test_Data' folder, and initiate system state recovery from an isolated offline storage platform.</p>
        </td></tr>
            </table>
